explanations.E:
(Choice E) Lidocaine can relax vascular smooth muscle via blockade of Na~ current mediated action
potentials. However, in this case, extravasation of norepinephrine is responsible for the vasoconstriction;
nerve blockade would not reverse the ischemia.

explanations.C:
(Choice C) Digoxin slows conduction through the atrioventricular node and is useful in treating
supraventricular tachycardia, especially atrial fibrillation. It causes a well-characterized toxicity in overdose;
symptoms include fatigue, yellow-tinted vision, nausea/vomiting, diarrhea, and confusion.
